SECURITY MODEL

PKVault must NOT be considered the authentication authority.

Do not expose PKVault directly to Vantafyn clients.

Do not require Vantafyn users to have PKVault accounts.

Do not expose PKVault publicly through the normal Vantafyn/Jellyfin domain as part of this architecture.

PKVault should ideally remain reachable only by the Jellyfin/Companion host through localhost, LAN, Docker networking, or another private server-side route.

All client-facing Pokémon API calls must go through Vantafyn Companion.

Vantafyn should continue using the existing Jellyfin authentication/token it already uses.

Every Companion Pokémon endpoint must identify the current Jellyfin user from the authenticated Jellyfin request.

Never trust a client-supplied Jellyfin user ID for authorization.

For example, do NOT accept:

POST /pokemon/transfer
{
"userId": "some-other-user"
}

and trust it.

The authenticated user must come from the Jellyfin server-side request context.

Admin-only actions must use the existing Jellyfin administrator/authorization mechanisms already appropriate to this plugin.

