SAVE FILE SAFETY

This is one of the most important requirements.

Never modify a Pokémon save while the associated game is actively using it.

The final system must support game/save locking.

At minimum, Companion should be architected so a Pokémon save can have states like:

AVAILABLE
ACTIVE_GAME_SESSION
LOCKED_FOR_OPERATION
ERROR
UNKNOWN

When a game is running:

READ operations may eventually be allowed if safe.

WRITE operations must be blocked.

The client should receive a clear reason such as:

"Finish and exit Pokémon Emerald before modifying this save."

Do not fake game-session detection if current infrastructure cannot reliably tell us this.

Instead introduce a clean abstraction/interface that can later be wired to the actual Games session tracking.

Save modification should eventually follow a transaction model:

1. Authenticate user.
2. Validate ownership.
3. Verify feature permission.
4. Verify game is not active.
5. Acquire save lock.
6. Verify source save.
7. Create backup.
8. Perform Pokémon operation through PKVault.
9. Validate operation result.
10. Write safely.
11. Prefer temporary write + atomic replacement where technically appropriate.
12. Verify result.
13. Record transaction/history.
14. Release lock.

If anything fails after modification begins:

Attempt rollback/restore from backup.

Do not leave partially modified saves.

Do not implement unsafe direct writes merely to make a demo work.

